// ProjectDeliveryS739 — Sprint 739: the Claude hooks are a member - dcHooksAreAMember, the ninth D0479 extraction and the first slice of dcKeelCliIsThinDispatch, chartered by D0479. The keel hook body (stop, post-edit, pre-bash, pre-write, config-change, subagent-stop, prompt - 1246 lines of main.rs), its override and ledger helpers, the two recall constants the prompt hook shares with keel recall and the two hook test modules are sliced out of keel-cli/src/main.rs into members/keel-hooks/src/lib.rs; shellcheck.rs and proactive.rs move beside them. find_repo_root and engine_version_skew, two dispatch-level helpers the hooks and the binary both call, descend to keel_process::workspace as pub must_use fns - a member cannot call into the binary. keel-cli's lib.rs re-exports keel_hooks as hooks and shellcheck and proactive at their old paths; main.rs imports the eight names it still calls. The hook dispatch line is unchanged and main.rs is outside the enforcement-surface lock, so D0511 (accepted under standing consent, #DependsOn d0479) records the layering with no marker. Three doc comments orphaned in main.rs by earlier moves are reattached to the fns they describe.. EXECUTE. 5 pts.
