    verification hooksAreAMemberRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "41bc5267-7028-4812-986b-0962636c1351"; :>> title = "Sprint 739 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-17"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Written at close-out, before the verifier is dispatched; avoidable issues scanned (issue011), each finding a tracked item or the reason it is not. (1) record task appends at the end of the def, so the split item landed at rank 26 below twenty-four items it now gates and was moved to rank 2 by a hand script (move739.py) - a backlog write the write lock and the record verb's validation never saw. Tracked: issue600, resolver dcRecordTaskPlacesTheItemBeforeANamedOne (added this sprint) - a --before flag that declares the item at its position. (2) The design inventory (block_deps.py) missed OVERRIDE_TTL_SECS because the const regex captured its trailing colon into the name, so the first build failed on one unpublished const and the script was reverted and re-applied; the build is the control that caught it and fired. Not tracked as an Issue: the inventory is a scratchpad script for a codemod that will be written once more (the parent), and a second miss of the same class would make it a pattern; the reconciliation line a codemod prints is where a names-the-staying-text-still-calls check belongs if it recurs. (3) Three doc comments were orphaned in main.rs before this sprint (cmd_check_engine's and keel gate --fast's above gate_subverb, keel why's above budget_arg) and the slice made the first two a three-doc merge on one fn; fixed in this commit by reattaching each to the fn it describes (redoc739.py, doc lines only, clippy clean). Not tracked: rustdoc has no lint for a doc that describes a different item and the parent sprint moves every remaining body out of main.rs, which is where the class ends. (4) The codemod's docstring said five names are published; the count was eight names imported from six fns and three consts by the time it applied clean - the dual-truth class in a comment. Fixed in this commit; not tracked: the reconciliation line prints the counts from the lists themselves, and the docstring now names the lists rather than restating a number that the line computes. (5) The backlog item was recorded after the code change was applied and verified, not before - recording rode with the sprint rather than ahead of it, and the DoD was written knowing the tree. Not a defect in the record (the DoD names the probes and both pass) but the order is the build-now-record-later shape; dcSprintNamesTheItemItDelivers on the frontier is the control that binds a sprint to an item, and this sprint's record names it. (6) The codemod applied clean on its third run with no fix-up pass after apply; the first two rounds were reverted whole by git checkout and git mv rather than patched in place, so the script is the only transform on the tree. Non-finding. (7) facts.py section 4's how-string cites keel-cli/src/shellcheck.rs by its old path while the fact itself reads the file through module_home (scripts/exec_brief/facts.py); the number is right and the citation is history. Not tracked separately: dcSourceCitationsOnTheLivingDocsResolve is the frontier item for stale path citations and this is one of its rows."; }
